# Proton Drive sync-conflict copies. The repo lives inside a synced folder, and
# the client has twice rolled a source file back and stashed the newer version
# under a name like "app (# Name clash 2026-07-25 n2epj7C #).js". Ignored so a
# stray copy can never be committed or bundled into a release zip — but note
# that seeing one means an edit may have been silently reverted, so check the
# working tree rather than just deleting it.
*# Name clash *

# Fusion native icons — copied at add-in startup from the Fusion install
